                     <msItem>
                        <author key="person_426">Beda etc</author>
                        <note>London, BL MSS Cotton Otho B.xi, Add. 34652 (fol. 2), and Cotton Otho
                           B.x (fols. 55, 58, and 62) were originally one volume. Now much burnt.
                           See Ker, <title>Catalogue of MSS containing Anglo-Saxon</title>, 230–234.
                           BL MS Add. 43703 is a copy of s. xvi (except of the leaf in Add
                           34652).</note>
                     </msItem>
                  </msContents>
                  <history>
                     <origin>
                        <origDate when-custom="0901/1025" notBefore="0901" notAfter="1025"
                           calendar="#gregorian">s. x-xi in.</origDate>
                     </origin>
                     <provenance source="6588"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_514">Southwick,
                           Hampshire. Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>A
                           Southwick inscription stretched across pp. 18–19 of the unburnt MS (see
                           Wanley in Bodleian Gough London 54). Part of another inscription occurs
                           at the foot of fol. 28: <q>fecerit quo minus eiusdem Ecclesie sit seu qui
                              hunc titulum dolo [...] deleuerit. nisi condigne eidem [...] Amen.
                              Amen</q> (s. xiii). Seen by <persName>Thomas Rudborne</persName> at
                           Southwick in s. xv (see Wharton, <title>Anglia Sacra</title>, i, 183).
                           Seen by <persName>Leland</persName> at Southwick (CBMLC
                        A31.3).</p></provenance>
                     <provenance cert="low" source="5744"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_437"
                           >Winchester, Hampshire. Benedictine cathedral priory of St Peter, St
                           Paul, and St Swithun</orgName><p>The Bede is in the same script as the
                           Parker Chronicle (CCCC 173) for the years 924–55, which was at
                           Winchester. The Chronicle is a copy of the Parker Chronicle to the year
                           1001.</p></provenance>
                     <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners"><p>Add. 34652 belonged to
                              <persName>Tanner</persName> and <persName>Th.
                        Astle</persName>.</p></provenance>
                  </history>
